# Ohrbound — Mobile Surface and Touch Proof

The Awtsmoos lets a whole world, an editor, and hidden advanced chambers rest within one narrow hand;
Awtsmoos.com now keeps each doorway reachable while no drawer or dialog escapes the land.

## Proven pre-change state

Forced DOM/CSS state inspection at 320px already showed zero horizontal document overflow and contained Advanced/dialog/editor geometry, but several critical controls were undersized: Sign in around 32px high, Advanced open/close 38px, dialog close about 34px, editor buttons about 41px, preference selects about 37px, brand link about 13px, and source HUD buttons about 35px.

The headless acceptance environment cannot create Ohrbound's WebGL renderer. The captured `Procedural Core WebGL could not initialize` exception is therefore an environment limitation for full game boot, not evidence against CSS containment. Surface verification bypassed renderer boot by applying the documented drawer/dialog/editor visual states directly.

## Isolated implementation

Only clean late-loaded `games/ohrbound/styles/polish.css` was rewritten. No renderer, physics, input, campaign, editor-state, API, or networking source changed.

The late polish layer now normalizes:
- brand/home target to minimum 44px high;
- Sign in to minimum 44px high;
- Advanced open/close to 44×44px;
- character dialog close to 44×44px;
- editor header/actions/palette buttons to minimum 44px high;
- preference selects to minimum 44px high;
- game HUD buttons to 44×44px.

Existing global motion already owns fine-pointer hover, button active state, focus, and reduced-motion behavior, so this pass intentionally did not duplicate that interaction logic.

## Final runtime geometry

390×844 forced visual state:
- document clientWidth/scrollWidth: 390/390;
- horizontal overflow: 0;
- Advanced overlay: 390×844;
- Advanced sheet: x=0..390 after 500ms transition settle;
- character dialog: x=8..360;
- editor toolbar/actions/grid: x=16..374;
- brand: 94×44;
- Sign in: 67×44;
- Advanced open/close: 44×44;
- dialog close: 44×44;
- preference select: 111×44;
- editor header/action: >=44px high;
- no visible critical target escaped a side edge.

320×568 forced visual state:
- document clientWidth/scrollWidth: 320/320;
- horizontal overflow: 0;
- Advanced overlay: 320×568;
- Advanced sheet: x=0..320 after settle;
- character dialog: x=8..290;
- editor toolbar/actions/grid: x=16..304;
- brand: 94×44;
- Sign in: 67×44;
- Advanced open/close: 44×44;
- dialog close: 44×44;
- preference select: 111×44;
- editor header/action: >=44px high;
- no visible critical target escaped a side edge.

The hidden HUD button measured 0×0 because the game pane cannot become active without WebGL in this browser. Source/cascade verification proves `.hud-button` now resolves to 44×44 when displayed, and later `hud-polish.css` does not override that size.

## Regression and source gates

- `polish.css`: 107 lines.
- no source line exceeds 160 characters.
- Ohrbound tests: 43/43 pass.
- no production logic changed.

## NEXT_ACTION

Audit the shared game player-shell launcher/menu because it appears across many games. Verify launcher and opened panel at 390×844 and 320×568, then repair shared interaction-state or containment defects once rather than repeating fixes route by route.
